    "message": "fix(cli): register a Pro stub for `goals`\n\n@ix/pro registers a plural list command alongside each singular manager\n— bug/bugs, plan/plans, task/tasks, goal/goals — and PRO_COMMANDS stubs\nevery one of those pairs except the last. `goal` was stubbed; `goals`\nwas not.\n\nSo on an OSS install `ix goals` fell through to commander and printed\n`error: unknown command 'goals'`. CLAUDE.md tells agents that a Pro-gated\ninstall is identified by the exact string `The '<name>' command requires\nIx Pro.`, and to stop retrying once they see it. An unrecognized\ncommander error gives them nothing to match, so the documented contract\nsimply did not hold for this one command.\n\nThis is only reachable from outside the OSS docs, which consistently say\n`ix goal list` — but `ix goals` is a real, fully implemented Pro command,\nso anyone who learned it on a Pro install, or any plugin that calls it,\nhits the wrong error.\n\nThe regression test now walks the singular/plural pairs explicitly rather\nthan listing commands one at a time, since listing is what let this one go\nmissing.",
